      "label": "Happy Afghan Stereotype",
      "description": "A derogatory stereotype implying that Afghans are inherently cheerful or carefree, often used to mock their perceived emotional instability or to trivialize their complex cultural and political realities. This stereotype is used in the meme to contrast with the 'Asad Afghan Taliban spokesman' persona, reinforcing a harmful narrative that reduces Afghan identity to emotional or behavioral caricatures.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
