    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5f11dc63",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the 'your girl broke up with you' scenario",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the scenario described in the bottom caption, 'but your girl broke up with you', which implies personal failure and emotional distress. This projection is onto the textual material that frames the meme's punchline, suggesting the user identifies with the emotional trigger (breakup) that leads to the exaggerated persona. The user is not directly projected onto a specific visual material (like a person) but onto the narrative context created by the text, which is a common feature in memes that use 'you' as a deictic to invite self-identification.",
